What:           /sys/class/leds/<DT-label>/timeout_abi
Date:           October 2026
Contact:        LieppOS GQ5012BF1 maintainers
Description:
                Read-only value 1 identifies the driver-owned timeout ABI.
                These attributes are installed in the LED's static group at
                registration; they are not recreated by trigger selection.
                The DT label and the regulator's voltage configuration are
                unchanged. No particular GQ5012BF1 label is asserted here.

What:           /sys/class/leds/<DT-label>/max_duration_ms
Date:           October 2026
Contact:        LieppOS GQ5012BF1 maintainers
Description:
                Read-only software ceiling, currently 5000 milliseconds.
                This is a provisional software protection policy, NOT a
                verified actuator thermal rating or deployment approval.

What:           /sys/class/leds/<DT-label>/duration_ms
Date:           October 2026
Contact:        LieppOS GQ5012BF1 maintainers
Description:
                Write decimal 1..max_duration_ms for an atomic bounded request;
                write 0 to cancel and acknowledge a recovered I/O fault.
                Negative/overflow/out-of-range input is rejected without
                replacing a previous request. The store detaches any existing
                LED trigger before taking the request mutex. No periodic or
                one-shot trigger is required or selected by this ABI.

                A CLOCK_BOOTTIME hrtimer is armed before regulator activation.
                Its callback queues kernel work; sleeping regulator operations
                run only in thread context. Replacement serializes and cancels
                the previous timer. Work checks the CURRENT absolute deadline,
                so a stale queued expiry cannot cancel a newer request.
                Last-request expiry does not depend on an open userspace fd,
                thread, process, Binder client or destructor.

                Read returns the requested remaining milliseconds (rounded up),
                zero if cancelled/expired/faulted. It is NOT physical motion or
                current feedback. Timer/workqueue scheduling is not hard realtime.

                Failed OFF latches a fault, rejects new ON, and retries every
                250ms while bound and running. Successful background cleanup
                does not clear the latch; an explicit successful 0 does.
                A blocked/suspended/stopping driver rejects positive requests.
                Resume never restores a pre-suspend request. Suspend requires
                checked OFF; failure aborts that suspend callback and retains
                the fault/retry path. Legacy nonzero brightness requests also
                get the finite software ceiling, not indefinite activation.

                The guarantee assumes a running kernel and working regulator
                operations on a dedicated controllable supply. Permanent PMIC
                errors, another consumer holding the rail, kernel hangs or
                forced device removal cannot be turned into physical OFF by
                software. Such errors remain visible, not successful OFF.

                Only the HAL's system UID/domain needs narrow duration_ms write
                and metadata read access; trigger/invert/delay/shot permissions
                are not required. No owner, mode or SELinux label is guessed or
                changed by the driver. Production activation remains gated.

What:           /sys/class/leds/<DT-label>/last_error
Date:           October 2026
Contact:        LieppOS GQ5012BF1 maintainers
Description:
                Read-only last negative errno, or zero. Reports asynchronous
                OFF failures and regulator fault notifications. A successful
                explicit OFF clears it; reading zero is not motion feedback.
                A failed remove/shutdown OFF is logged critically; Linux driver
                removal does not guarantee that returning an error prevents
                unbind. Hardware-off proof therefore still requires validation.
